WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.722
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:06.022 --> 00:00:09.420
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:16.169
Unit twenty: Friendship Challenges. Today you will talk about solving problems with the first conditional.

4
00:00:16.469 --> 00:00:19.156
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.275
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.117 --> 00:00:24.874
Friendship.

7
00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:28.823
Friendship means a relationship between friends.

8
00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:31.532
Our friendship started in grade seven.

9
00:00:32.117 --> 00:00:34.490
Your turn. Say: Friendship.

10
00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:38.195
Friendship.

11
00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:39.928
Argument.

12
00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:44.309
Argument means an angry talk between people who disagree.

13
00:00:44.917 --> 00:00:46.800
We had an argument about a game.

14
00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:49.628
Your turn. Say: Argument.

15
00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:53.270
Argument.

16
00:00:54.017 --> 00:00:54.832
Trust.

17
00:00:55.817 --> 00:00:58.559
Trust means believing that someone is honest.

18
00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:00.778
Trust takes time to build.

19
00:01:01.383 --> 00:01:03.699
Your turn. Say: Trust.

20
00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:07.349
Trust.

21
00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:09.363
Apologize.

22
00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.640
Apologize means to say sorry.

23
00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.099
I apologized for being late.

24
00:01:15.683 --> 00:01:18.266
Your turn. Say: Apologize.

25
00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.461
Apologize.

26
00:01:23.217 --> 00:01:24.136
Forgive.

27
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.626
Forgive means to stop being angry with someone.

28
00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:29.984
She forgave me the next day.

29
00:01:30.583 --> 00:01:32.713
Your turn. Say: Forgive.

30
00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:36.405
Forgive.

31
00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.047
Jealous.

32
00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:42.013
Jealous means unhappy because someone has what you want.

33
00:01:42.617 --> 00:01:44.454
I felt jealous of his new phone.

34
00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:47.691
Your turn. Say: Jealous.

35
00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:51.442
Jealous.

36
00:01:52.183 --> 00:01:53.242
Communicate.

37
00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:57.074
Communicate means to share ideas and feelings.

38
00:01:57.683 --> 00:01:59.718
Good friends communicate honestly.

39
00:02:00.317 --> 00:02:02.888
Your turn. Say: Communicate.

40
00:02:05.733 --> 00:02:06.723
Communicate.

41
00:02:07.483 --> 00:02:08.310
Support.

42
00:02:09.317 --> 00:02:12.013
Support means to help and encourage someone.

43
00:02:12.617 --> 00:02:14.082
Friends support each other.

44
00:02:14.683 --> 00:02:16.825
Your turn. Say: Support.

45
00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:20.528
Support.

46
00:02:21.333 --> 00:02:24.601
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:28.451
Visal, you look sad. What's wrong?

48
00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:34.269
I had an argument with my best friend. I said something unkind.

49
00:02:35.383 --> 00:02:36.617
What will you do?

50
00:02:37.717 --> 00:02:41.226
If I apologize, my friend will forgive me, I hope.

51
00:02:42.317 --> 00:02:44.548
And if you communicate honestly?

52
00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:49.554
If we talk, we will understand each other and rebuild trust.

53
00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:52.421
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:53.283 --> 00:02:55.736
Grammar focus: If plus present, will.

55
00:02:56.036 --> 00:02:57.188
Look at the pattern.

56
00:02:57.883 --> 00:03:00.545
If I apologize, my friend will forgive me.

57
00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.914
If we talk, we will understand each other.

58
00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:07.002
If you feel jealous, it will pass.

59
00:03:07.967 --> 00:03:11.684
Use the present simple after 'if', and 'will' in the result part.

60
00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:16.705
Be careful! Don't say: If I will apologize, my friend will forgive me.

61
00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:21.665
Say: If I apologize, my friend will forgive me.

62
00:03:21.965 --> 00:03:24.045
Use the present simple after 'if'.

63
00:03:24.833 --> 00:03:27.253
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:29.393
Fixing a Friendship.

65
00:03:29.693 --> 00:03:31.553
Every friendship has challenges.

66
00:03:32.567 --> 00:03:35.750
An argument can hurt trust, and feeling jealous is normal.

67
00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:39.730
Good friends communicate honestly and support each other.

68
00:03:40.733 --> 00:03:44.718
If you apologize sincerely, your friend will probably forgive you.

69
00:03:45.733 --> 00:03:48.708
If we keep talking, our friendship will grow stronger.

70
00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:53.558
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:54.417 --> 00:03:56.892
If I apologize, she blank forgive me.

72
00:03:57.192 --> 00:04:00.021
A, will. B, would. C, is.

73
00:04:03.567 --> 00:04:05.276
The answer is A: will.

74
00:04:06.417 --> 00:04:08.857
To stop being angry with someone is to blank.

75
00:04:09.157 --> 00:04:12.997
A, forgive. B, apologize. C, argue.

76
00:04:16.533 --> 00:04:18.266
The answer is A: forgive.

77
00:04:19.417 --> 00:04:21.753
Believing that someone is honest is blank.

78
00:04:22.053 --> 00:04:25.579
A, trust. B, jealousy. C, support.

79
00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:31.017
The answer is A: trust.

80
00:04:32.233 --> 00:04:35.385
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:38.296
How do you fix a problem with a friend?

82
00:04:47.083 --> 00:04:48.560
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:57.062
I talk to my friend and say sorry if I made a mistake. If we communicate honestly, we will understand each other.

84
00:04:57.362 --> 00:04:59.060
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:03.949
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and if plus present, will.

86
00:05:04.249 --> 00:05:08.864
Today's value is loyalty. Stand by your friends in good times and bad times.

87
00:05:09.164 --> 00:05:12.094
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

88
00:05:12.394 --> 00:05:15.116
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

